<article class="prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">About the journal</p>
  <h1>Listening past<br><em>the first impression.</em></h1>
  <p class="lede">Eva’s Earworms is a place for the songs that lodge somewhere between memory and muscle.</p>
  <p>Each note begins with close listening: a returning phrase, an unexpected texture, a rhythm that alters the room. The aim is not to score music or settle its meaning, but to notice what makes a track stay.</p>
  <aside class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <h2 id="principles-title">House rules</h2>
    <ul><li><strong>Listen closely.</strong> Separate documented facts from interpretation.</li><li><strong>Keep it human.</strong> No rankings engineered for outrage.</li><li><strong>Travel light.</strong> No ads, trackers, or autoplay.</li></ul>
  </aside>
</article>
